Model the demand that occurs before replacement becomes usable (@cs-uncertain-lead: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Inventory-Analytics-Rossi.lingua#r_61Y17EAC05XZSS1B28NX17SV7C", #source "../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8", #source "../sources/Good-Storage-and-Distribution-WHO.lingua#r_64EPQ96J7NE7QCWQ28SPXJ8V4D", #chemical-supply-systems "An-inspectable-exact-replenishment-demand-distribution.lingua#r_6EXE7DWBBK7BSDWM5675JY6X4H") { r_7KV83BXJ1Q08JHFD9ZAC9ERTK6
**Read:** [Inventory Analytics — Roberto Rossi](../sources/Inventory-Analytics-Rossi.lingua#r_61Y17EAC05XZSS1B28NX17SV7C), the entire Stochastic Inventory Control chapter and relevant appendix; [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), complete stochastic-inventory and lead-time material; [Good storage and distribution practices for medical products — WHO](../sources/Good-Storage-and-Distribution-WHO.lingua#r_64EPQ96J7NE7QCWQ28SPXJ8V4D), complete status, rotation and condition requirements.

Define demand during replenishment as the total requirement between the ordering decision and usable replacement. If daily demands are independent and identically distributed with mean μ and variance σ², and the integer lead time L is independent of them, then E[Dᴸ]=μE[L] and Var(Dᴸ)=σ²E[L]+μ²Var(L). Derive these statements using conditioning on L before applying them.

Work a finite distribution exactly and compare it with an assumed normal approximation. State which service event is being modelled: under a particular continuous-review cycle model, a reorder point may be chosen from a lead-demand quantile. Cycle service, expected shortage and fill fraction still require their own policy context. Do not interpret a single quantile as a universal plant-uptime guarantee.

Investigate dependence, intermittent demand, variable lot release and correlated delays. A larger safety stock can increase age and capacity pressure. Compare moving inventory nearer to the user, shortening a testing delay, improving delivery reliability and holding a reserve, using the same measurable service requirement. The next original program calculates the exact finite-mixture distribution under explicit independence assumptions; the later empirical/academic work tests how well those assumptions represent the actual chemical supply.

**Continue:** [Calculate an exact finite replenishment-demand distribution and test it independently](An-inspectable-exact-replenishment-demand-distribution.lingua#r_6EXE7DWBBK7BSDWM5675JY6X4H).

